n":"A village in the New Forest in Hampshire, England.","example":null,"frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"bank|proper_noun|1","lemma":"bank","norm":"bank","pos":"proper_noun","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","cat:en:places in england","cat:en:places in hampshire, england","cat:en:villages in england","cat:en:villages in hampshire, england","pos_raw:name"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":4,"word":"bank"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"A major London Underground station in the City of London, named after the Bank of England and one of the busiest stations on the network (OS grid ref TQ3281)","example":"Anybody familiar with the London Underground network will know that Bank Tube station is a place to be avoided - if at all possible - on a weekday morning. Located at the very heart of London's 'Square Mile' financial district, some 70,000 people detrain there during the morning peak, to pass through its gatelines and those at the adjoining station at Monument. A further 50,000 passengers squeeze into the station complex at exactly the same time of day, in order to change between the five lines that pass through it.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"bank|proper_noun|2","lemma":"bank","norm":"bank","pos":"proper_noun","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:name"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":4,"word":"bank"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"A surname.","example":null,"frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"bank|proper_noun|3","lemma":"bank","norm":"bank","pos":"proper_noun","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:2","cat:en:english surnames","pos_raw:name"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":4,"word":"bank"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(following a noun) Having partitive effect. — Indicates a given part.","example":"We want a larger slice of the cake.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|24","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","qual:following a noun","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(except in phrases, dialectal, obsolete) Expressing distance or motion. — From (a place); off.","example":"Take the chicken out of the freezer.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|1","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","tag:dialectal","tag:obsolete","qual:except in phrases","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(obsolete except in phrases) Expressing distance or motion. — Since, from (a given time, earlier state etc.).","example":"He hasn't been well of late.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|2","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","qual:obsolete except in phrases","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing distance or motion. — From, away from (a position, number, distance etc.).","example":"There are no shops within twenty miles of the cottage.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|3","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing separation. — Indicating removal, absence or separation, with the action indicated by a transitive verb and the quality or substance by a grammatical object.","example":"Finally she was relieved of the burden of caring for her sick husband.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|4","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing separation. — Indicating removal, absence or separation, with resulting state indicated by an adjective.","example":"He seemed devoid of human feelings.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|5","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(obsolete) Expressing separation. — Indicating removal, absence or separation, construed with an intransitive verb.","example":"He was kindly treated by the people at Saco, and recovered of his wounds.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|6","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","tag:obsolete","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing origin. — Indicating an ancestral source or origin of descent.","example":"The word is believed to be of Japanese origin.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|7","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing origin. — Introducing an epithet that indicates a birthplace, residence, dominion, or other place associated with the individual.","example":"Jesus of Nazareth (after hometown)","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|8","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing origin. — Indicating a (non-physical) source of action or emotion; introducing a cause, instigation; from, out of, as an expression of.","example":"The invention was born of necessity.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|9","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(following an intransitive verb) Expressing origin. — Indicates the source or cause of the verb.","example":"It is said that she died of a broken heart.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|10","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","qual:following an intransitive verb","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(following an adjective) Expressing origin. — Indicates the subject or cause of the adjective.","example":"I am tired of all this nonsense.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|11","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","qual:following an adjective","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(following a passive verb) Expressing agency. — Indicates the agent (for most verbs, now usually expressed with by).","example":"I am not particularly enamoured of this idea.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|12","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","qual:following a passive verb","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing agency. — Used to introduce the \"subjective genitive\"; following a noun to form the head of a postmodifying noun phrase (see also 'Possession' senses below).","example":"The contract can be terminated at any time with the agreement of both parties.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|13","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(following an adjective) Expressing agency. — Used to indicate the agent of something described by the adjective.","example":"It was very brave of you to speak out like that.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|14","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","qual:following an adjective","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(making etc.) Expressing composition, substance. — Used to indicate the material or substance used.","example":"Many 'corks' are now actually made of plastic.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|15","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","rtag:after a verb expressing construction","qual:making etc.","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(directly following a noun) Expressing composition, substance. — Used to indicate the material of the just-mentioned object.","example":"She wore a dress of silk.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|16","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","qual:directly following a noun","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing composition, substance. — Indicating the composition of a given collective or quantitative noun.","example":"I'll have a dozen of those apples, please.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|17","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing composition, substance. — Used to link a given class of things with a specific example of that class.","example":"Welcome to the historic town of Harwich.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|18","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing composition, substance. — Links two nouns in near-apposition, with the first qualifying the second; \"which is also\".","example":"I'm not driving this wreck of a car.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|19","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Introducing subject matter. — Links an intransitive verb, or a transitive verb and its subject (especially verbs to do with thinking, feeling, expressing etc.), with its subject-matter; concerning, with regard to.","example":"I'm always thinking of you.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|20","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(following a noun (now chiefly nouns of knowledge, communication etc.)) Introducing subject matter. — Introduces its subject matter; about, concerning.","example":"He told us the story of his journey to India.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|21","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","qual:following a noun (now chiefly nouns of knowledge, communication etc.)","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(following an adjective) Introducing subject matter. — Introduces its subject matter.","example":"This behaviour is typical of teenagers.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|22","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","qual:following an adjective","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(following a number or other quantitive word) Having partitive effect. — Introduces the whole for which is indicated only the specified part or segment; \"from among\".","example":"Most of these apples are rotten.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|23","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","qual:following a number or other quantitive word","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(or as a predicate after to be, archaic, literary) Having partitive effect. — Some, an amount of, one of.","example":"On the whole, they seem to be of the decent sort.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|25","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","tag:archaic","tag:literary","rtag:with preceding partitive word assumed","qual:or as a predicate after to be","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Having partitive effect. — Links to a genitive noun or possessive pronoun, with partitive effect (though now often merged with possessive senses, below; see also double possessive).","example":"He is a friend of mine.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"id":"of|preposition|26","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"sourc