he subject or cause of the adjective.","example":"I am tired of all this nonsense.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|11","lemma":"of","mw":false,"norm":"of","pos":"preposition","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","qual:following an adjective","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"(following a passive verb) Expressing agency. — Indicates the agent (for most verbs, now usually expressed with by).","example":"I am not particularly enamoured of this idea.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|12","lemma":"of","mw":false,"norm":"of","pos":"preposition","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","qual:following a passive verb","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing agency. — Used to introduce the \"subjective genitive\"; following a noun to form the head of a postmodifying noun phrase (see also 'Possession' senses below).","example":"The contract can be terminated at any time with the agreement of both parties.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|13","lemma":"of","mw":false,"norm":"of","pos":"preposition","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"(following an adjective) Expressing agency. — Used to indicate the agent of something described by the adjective.","example":"It was very brave of you to speak out like that.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|14","lemma":"of","mw":false,"norm":"of","pos":"preposition","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","qual:following an adjective","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"(making etc.) Expressing composition, substance. — Used to indicate the material or substance used.","example":"Many 'corks' are now actually made of plastic.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|15","lemma":"of","mw":false,"norm":"of","pos":"preposition","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","rtag:after a verb expressing construction","qual:making etc.","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"(directly following a noun) Expressing composition, substance. — Used to indicate the material of the just-mentioned object.","example":"She wore a dress of silk.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|16","lemma":"of","mw":false,"norm":"of","pos":"preposition","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","qual:directly following a noun","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing composition, substance. — Indicating the composition of a given collective or quantitative noun.","example":"I'll have a dozen of those apples, please.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|17","lemma":"of","mw":false,"norm":"of","pos":"preposition","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing composition, substance. — Used to link a given class of things with a specific example of that class.","example":"Welcome to the historic town of Harwich.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|18","lemma":"of","mw":false,"norm":"of","pos":"preposition","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing composition, substance. — Links two nouns in near-apposition, with the first qualifying the second; \"which is also\".","example":"I'm not driving this wreck of a car.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|19","lemma":"of","mw":false,"norm":"of","pos":"preposition","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"Introducing subject matter. — Links an intransitive verb, or a transitive verb and its subject (especially verbs to do with thinking, feeling, expressing etc.), with its subject-matter; concerning, with regard to.","example":"I'm always thinking of you.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|20","lemma":"of","mw":false,"norm":"of","pos":"preposition","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"(following a noun (now chiefly nouns of knowledge, communication etc.)) Introducing subject matter. — Introduces its subject matter; about, concerning.","example":"He told us the story of his journey to India.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|21","lemma":"of","mw":false,"norm":"of","pos":"preposition","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","qual:following a noun (now chiefly nouns of knowledge, communication etc.)","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"(following an adjective) Introducing subject matter. — Introduces its subject matter.","example":"This behaviour is typical of teenagers.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792285133262,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|22","lemma":"of","mw":false,"nor