ns, usually with verbs of receiving (such as get or find) or sensing (such as see or hear), typically stating the existence or typicality of something.","example":"You get a lot of rude people in London.","frame_run_id":38,"frame_seq":37,"frame_ts_ms":1792292295353,"id":"you|pronoun|8","lemma":"you","norm":"you","pos":"pronoun","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","tag:indefinite","tag:nominative","tag:objective","tag:personal","tag:plural","tag:pronoun","tag:second-person","tag:singular","pos_raw:pron"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":["ye"],"token_index":5,"word":"you"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"The individual or group spoken or written to.","example":"Have you gentlemen come to see the lady who fell backwards off a bus?","frame_run_id":38,"frame_seq":37,"frame_ts_ms":1792292295353,"id":"you|determiner|1","lemma":"you","norm":"you","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:det"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"you"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used before epithets, describing the person being addressed, for emphasis.","example":"You idiot!","frame_run_id":38,"frame_seq":37,"frame_ts_ms":1792292295353,"id":"you|determiner|2","lemma":"you","norm":"you","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:det"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"you"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(transitive) To address (a person) using the pronoun you (in the past, especially to use you rather than thou, when you was considered more formal).","example":"Youing consists in relating everything in the conversation to the person you wish to flatter, and introducing the word “you” into your speech as often as possible.","frame_run_id":38,"frame_seq":37,"frame_ts_ms":1792292295353,"id":"you|verb|1","lemma":"you","norm":"you","pos":"verb","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","tag:transitive","pos_raw:verb"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"you"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"The name of the Latin