ducing the word “you” into your speech as often as possible.","frame_run_id":38,"frame_seq":37,"frame_ts_ms":1792292295353,"id":"you|verb|1","lemma":"you","norm":"you","pos":"verb","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","tag:transitive","pos_raw:verb"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"you"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"The name of the Latin-script letter U/u.","example":"‘Eff. You. En,’ said Mr Banstead. ‘Fun![…]’","frame_run_id":38,"frame_seq":37,"frame_ts_ms":1792292295353,"id":"you|noun|1","lemma":"you","norm":"you","pos":"noun","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:2","pos_raw:noun"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"you"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(interrogative, not-comparable) To what degree or extent.","example":"How often do you practice?","frame_run_id":38,"frame_seq":37,"frame_ts_ms":1792292295353,"id":"how|adverb|1","lemma":"how","norm":"how","pos":"adverb","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","tag:interrogative","tag:not-comparable","pos_raw:adv"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":0,"word":"how"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(interrogative, not-comparable) In what manner","example":"Economics is a messy discipline: too fluid to be a science, too rigorous to be an art. Perhaps it is fitting that economists’ most-used metric, gross domestic product (GDP), is a tangle too.[…]But as a foundation for analysis it is highly subjective: it rests on difficult decisions about what counts as a territory, what counts as output and how to value it. Indeed, economists are still tweaking it.","frame_run_id":38,"frame_seq":37,"frame_ts_ms":1792292295353,"id":"how|adverb|2","lemma":"how","norm":"how","pos":"adverb","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","tag:interrogative","tag:not-comparable","pos_raw:adv"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":0,"word":"how"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(interrogative, not-comparable) In what manner: — By what means.","example":"How do you solve this puzzle?","frame_run_id":38,"fram