nt of, one of.","example":"On the whole, they seem to be of the decent sort.","frame_run_id":90,"frame_seq":89,"frame_ts_ms":1792292397291,"id":"of|preposition|25","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","tag:archaic","tag:literary","rtag:with preceding partitive word assumed","qual:or as a predicate after to be","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":4,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Having partitive effect. — Links to a genitive noun or possessive pronoun, with partitive effect (though now often merged with possessive senses, below; see also double possessive).","example":"He is a friend of mine.","frame_run_id":90,"frame_seq":89,"frame_ts_ms":1792292397291,"id":"of|preposition|26","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":4,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing possession. — Belonging to, existing in, or taking place in a given location, place or time. Compare \"origin\" senses, above.","example":"He was perhaps the most famous scientist of the twentieth century.","frame_run_id":90,"frame_seq":89,"frame_ts_ms":1792292397291,"id":"of|preposition|27","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":4,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing possession. — Belonging to (a place) through having title, ownership or control over it.","example":"The owner of the nightclub was arrested.","frame_run_id":90,"frame_seq":89,"frame_ts_ms":1792292397291,"id":"of|preposition|28","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":4,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing possession. — Belonging to (someone or something) as something they possess or have as a characteristic; the \"possessive genitive\". (With abstract nouns, this intersects with the subjective genitive, above under \"agency\" senses.)","example":"Keep the handle of the saucepan away from the flames.","frame_run_id":90,"frame_seq":89,"frame_ts_ms":1792292397291,"id":"of|preposition|29","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":4,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Forming the \"objective genitive\".","example":null,"frame_run_id":90,"frame_seq":89,"frame_ts_ms":1792292397291,"id":"of|preposition|30","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":4,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Forming the \"objective genitive\". — Follows an agent noun, verbal noun or noun of action.","example":"She had a profound distrust of the police.","frame_run_id":90,"frame_seq":89,"frame_ts_ms":1792292397291,"id":"of|preposition|31","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":4,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(archaic, literary) Expressing qualities or characteristics. — Links an adjective with a noun or noun phrase to form a quasi-adverbial qualifier; in respect to, as regards.","example":"My companion seemed affable and easy of manner.","frame_run_id":90,"frame_seq":89,"frame_ts_ms":1792292397291,"id":"of|preposition|32","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","tag:archaic","tag:literary","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":4,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing qualities or characteristics. — Indicates a quality or characteristic; \"characterized by\".","example":"Pooh was said to be a bear of very little brain.","frame_run_id":90,"frame_seq":89,"frame_ts_ms":1792292397291,"id":"of|preposition|33","lemma":"of","nor