 effect. — Introduces the whole for which is indicated only the specified part or segment; \"from among\".","example":"Most of these apples are rotten.","frame_run_id":90,"frame_seq":89,"frame_ts_ms":1792292397291,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|23","lemma":"of","mw":false,"norm":"of","pos":"preposition","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","qual:following a number or other quantitive word","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"(or as a predicate after to be, archaic, literary) Having partitive effect. — Some, an amount of, one of.","example":"On the whole, they seem to be of the decent sort.","frame_run_id":90,"frame_seq":89,"frame_ts_ms":1792292397291,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|25","lemma":"of","mw":false,"norm":"of","pos":"preposition","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","tag:archaic","tag:literary","rtag:with preceding partitive word assumed","qual:or as a predicate after to be","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"Having partitive effect. — Links to a genitive noun or possessive pronoun, with partitive effect (though now often merged with possessive senses, below; see also double possessive).","example":"He is a friend of mine.","frame_run_id":90,"frame_seq":89,"frame_ts_ms":1792292397291,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|26","lemma":"of","mw":false,"norm":"of","pos":"preposition","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing possession. — Belonging to, existing in, or taking place in a given location, place or time. Compare \"origin\" senses, above.","example":"He was perhaps the most famous scientist of the twentieth century.","frame_run_id":90,"frame_seq":89,"frame_ts_ms":1792292397291,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|27","lemma":"of","mw":false,"norm":"of","pos":"preposition","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing possession. — Belonging to (a place) through having title, ownership or control over it.","example":"The owner of the nightclub was arrested.","frame_run_id":90,"frame_seq":89,"frame_ts_ms":1792292397291,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|28","lemma":"of","mw":false,"norm":"of","pos":"preposition","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing possession. — Belonging to (someone or something) as something they possess or have as a characteristic; the \"possessive genitive\". (With abstract nouns, this intersects with the subjective genitive, above under \"agency\" senses.)","example":"Keep the handle of the saucepan away from the flames.","frame_run_id":90,"frame_seq":89,"frame_ts_ms":1792292397291,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|29","lemma":"of","mw":false,"norm":"of","pos":"preposition","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"Forming the \"objective genitive\".","example":null,"frame_run_id":90,"frame_seq":89,"frame_ts_ms":1792292397291,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|30","lemma":"of","mw":false,"norm":"of","pos":"preposition","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"Forming the \"objective genitive\". — Follows an agent noun, verbal noun or noun of action.","example":"She had a profound distrust of the police.","frame_run_id":90,"frame_seq":89,"frame_ts_ms":1792292397291,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|31","lemma":"of","mw":false,"norm":"of","pos":"preposition","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"sema